  "profile": "Keyless; bundled Polish fast. Best is an offline ablation (11,978,867 bytes; SHA256 e80cc4cefbdface06e9223f43f089556b9dcf104020fbc0a200f6863c57d4405). No dependency changes.",
  "method": "One frozen two-worker CLI baseline. Replayed the extra branch point on its outputs and OCR boxes. Matching branch points reused baseline bytes. Fresh CLI validated the changed PDFs in each arm. Compared identifiers with exact values and owner, including printed country prefixes. Owner records are complete transfer objects and individual complete appeal or mandate party records. The bootstrap samples complete cases 1,200 times with seed 87.",
  "families": "Disjoint source cases in the seeded schedule. Calibration families were single-column, reordered and two-column. No fitted model or corpus-based threshold tuning. Synonyms, alternative-formats and scan are held-out families; all are from the same generator. The printed-value retention path was assessed after the strict decoder ablation, so this is development evidence.",
  "printed_value_policy": "The alternative-only arm made zero changes in every cohort. The fast and best arms also retain a fully legible original that the earlier checksum normalizer discarded when the complete raw field has an independent owner binding and every crop symbol strongly agrees. No checksum-invalid alternative can correct any digit.",
